{"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline"],"anchor":"Essentials","generated":true,"title":"Essentials"}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"anatomy-of-a-game.png","type":"image"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A Gnusto game is one type conforming to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Game","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":". That one type carries everything: the rooms and things, where they start, and the rules that govern them. This article is the model underneath — how the engine finds your declarations, how one value is both a declaration and a live reference, and how the world that never changes is kept apart from the state that does.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Declarations are stored properties","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Declarations-are-stored-properties"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Rooms, things, and custom state are declared as ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"stored properties"}]},{"text":" of the game type:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["struct OperaHouse: Game {","    let foyer = Location { name(\"Foyer of the Opera House\") }","    let bar   = Location { name(\"Foyer Bar\"); dark }","    let cloak = Item { name(\"velvet cloak\"); wearable }","    @Global var disturbances = 0","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When you construct the world with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameWorld\/init(game:saveDirectory:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", the engine’s bootstrap reflects over the game value with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Mirror"},{"text":" and collects every ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Global","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":". It names each entity after the property it was stored in: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"foyer"},{"text":" becomes ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/EntityID","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"foyer\""},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cloak"},{"text":" becomes ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"cloak\""},{"text":", and so on. You never write these IDs by hand — the property name ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"is"}]},{"text":" the name.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This is why declarations must live in the type’s main body, not an extension: Swift only allows stored properties there, and the Mirror only sees stored properties. (When even the declarations need to span files or ship separately, that is what a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameContent","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" bundle is for — see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContentBundles","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"One value, two roles","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"One-value-two-roles"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A declaration and a live reference are the ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"same value"}]},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let cloak = Item { name(\"velvet cloak\"); wearable }   \/\/ the declaration","","\/\/ …later, inside a rule body:","cloak.after(.take) {","    if cloak.isWorn { … }        \/\/ the live reference — reads current state","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cloak"},{"text":" is an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" value. Written in the game body it ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"declares"}]},{"text":" the cloak. Used in a rule it ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"reads and writes the live cloak’s state"}]},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/isWorn","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/isHeld","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/name","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", and so on all consult the current turn.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This works because each ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" mints a private identity token when it is created. The token — not the struct’s contents — is the entity’s identity, and it survives copying. Two items are equal when they share a token (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/==(_:_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"). Inside a turn, the token resolves to the entity’s ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/EntityID","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" and then to its state; outside a turn there is no state to read, so a live property access traps with an explanation rather than returning a meaningless value.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"References are always compile-checked. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cloak.after(.take)"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hook.holds(cloak)"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"foyer.north(bar)"},{"text":" — every one is ordinary property access, so renaming a room or deleting an item breaks the build instead of the running game.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Scenery","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Scenery"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every noun a room description names should answer when the player examines it. Declare a fixture with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/scenery(_:adjectives:synonyms:description:_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let wall = Item.scenery(","    \"stone wall\", adjectives: \"rough\", synonyms: \"masonry\", \"old brickwork\",","    description: \"Mortar fills the cracks.\")"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This creates an ordinary ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" with a name, vocabulary, examine text, and the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/scenery","type":"reference"},{"text":" trait. The fixture cannot be taken and gets no stock room-listing sentence. The name and synonyms contribute nouns and adjectives through the usual parser rules: ","type":"text"},{"code":"stone wall","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" answers to ","type":"text"},{"code":"wall","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"stone wall","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; ","type":"text"},{"code":"old brickwork","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" adds "},{"code":"brickwork","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and the adjective "},{"code":"old","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"adjectives:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"synonyms:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are variadic, so they read the way ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/adjectives(_:)","isActive":true},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/synonyms(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" read inside an "},{"code":"Item { }","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" block — one phrase per argument, no brackets. A synonym is a noun phrase, not a single word, which is why "},{"code":"old brickwork","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" above counts as one argument."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A phrase that ends in one of the item’s "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"nouns"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is a name, and names are matched first. A phrase that doesn’t — "},{"code":"x rough","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"take velvet","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — is a "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"description","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", and the parser answers one when it picks out exactly one thing in view and asks ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"“Which do you mean…?”"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" when it picks out several. Second pass, always: a description can never take a phrase away from something that already answered to it as a name.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Store it on your game or content bundle and place it in ","type":"text"},{"code":"map","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", just like any other item:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["var map: WorldMap {","    player.starts(in: hall)","    wall.starts(in: hall)","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"All arguments after the name are optional. Use the trailing trait block when scenery has another role:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let niche = Item.scenery(\"shadowed niche\", synonyms: \"alcove\") {","    container","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The niche can hold things and take item rules. For text that turns on the niche’s own state — open or shut, lit or dark — omit ","type":"text"},{"code":"description:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and put "},{"code":"description(when: \\.isOpen, …, otherwise: …)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in the trait block; for text that depends on anything else, attach a "},{"code":"niche.describe { … }","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" rule. Without any description, examining it uses the game’s stock examine line. Placement determines where a piece of scenery is visible, just as it does for other items."}]},{"anchor":"The-parts-of-the-Game-protocol","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"The parts of the `Game` protocol"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Game","isActive":true},{"text":" gathers a handful of members, most with defaults so a small game declares only what it needs:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"title","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"intro"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tagline"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxScore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — the banner and scoring metadata."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"map","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — geography and initial placement, as a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WorldMap","type":"reference"},{"text":". Read once at startup to build the initial state.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"rules","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — all game logic, as a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Rules","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" value. Defaults to empty."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"verbs","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — player-typeable verbs this game adds, as "},{"code":"[SyntaxRule]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Defaults to empty. See "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AddingCustomVerbs","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"content","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — content bundles the game composes itself from, as "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameContents","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". Defaults to empty. See "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContentBundles","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"noiseWords","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — filler words the parser drops from input before matching, beside the built-in articles, as "},{"code":"[String]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A spell game adds "},{"code":"\"spell\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" so "},{"code":"cast the glow spell","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" parses as "},{"code":"cast glow","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Defaults to empty; a noise word that is also a verb, preposition, direction, item word, or one of the words the parser claims for itself — the pronouns, the multi-object keywords, the conjunction, the exception words, the possessives — is a fatal diagnostic, since stripping it would make the word untypeable."}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The protocol extension also hands every game three ambient references usable as bare identifiers inside "},{"code":"map","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"rules","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" blocks:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"player"},{"text":" — the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Player","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", for its location, score, and inventory, and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Player\/item","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" for the player as a thing in the world (what ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"X ME"},{"text":" examines).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"world"},{"type":"text","text":" — the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/World","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", for rules that apply everywhere (like daemons)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"command"},{"type":"text","text":" — the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Command","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" currently being performed, inside a rule body."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"The-map-block","level":2,"text":"The `map` block","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map"},{"text":" is a result-builder property that yields a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WorldMap"},{"text":" — a flat list of ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/MapEntry"},{"text":" statements: exits, initial item placements, and the player’s start.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var map: WorldMap {","    foyer.south(bar)                 \/\/ an exit","    bar.north(foyer)                 \/\/ and the way back, stated separately","","    player.starts(in: foyer)         \/\/ where the player begins","    cloak.startsWorn                 \/\/ where each thing begins","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Exits are one-way, so an asymmetric map needs no special case. There are five kinds of exit and eight ways to place a thing; ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WorldMapAndExits"},{"text":" covers all of them.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Immutable-definition-mutable-state","level":2,"text":"Immutable definition, mutable state","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Internally, the engine keeps two things strictly apart:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"definition"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" is everything that never changes during play: names, descriptions, exits, rules, and the parser’s vocabulary. It is built once, from your declarations, at startup.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"state","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" is everything that ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"does"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" change: where each item is, what is lit, the score, the turn count, which things have been touched, and your ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Global"},{"text":" values.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The entire mutable state is a single ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"text":" value. Every change funnels through it, so a turn commits atomically at its end (see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline"},{"text":") and save\/restore is a serialization call rather than a feature threaded through the codebase.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When you write ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cloak.isWorn"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"player.score += 1"},{"text":" in a rule, you are reading and writing that one state value through the entity’s token — never touching the definition, and never seeing another turn’s half-finished changes.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"See-also","level":2,"text":"See also","type":"heading"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GettingStarted","type":"reference"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline","isActive":true}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WritingRules","isActive":true}]}]}]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/gnusto\/anatomyofagame"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto"],["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/BootstrapDiagnostics"],["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WorldMapAndExits"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"How a single Swift type becomes a world the engine can run.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AnatomyOfAGame"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"kind":"article","metadata":{"role":"article","title":"Anatomy of a Game","modules":[{"name":"Gnusto"}],"roleHeading":"Article"},"references":{"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Player":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Player"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Player","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/player","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Player"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Player","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The player character, available as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"player"},{"text":" inside any computed property","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Game"},{"text":" type.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Player/item":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The player as a thing in the world — what "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"X ME"},{"type":"text","text":" resolves to, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"where per-game text and rules about the player’s own body hang:"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Player\/item","title":"item","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/player\/item","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"item"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Item","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto4ItemV"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/TheTurnPipeline":{"role":"article","title":"The Turn Pipeline","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/theturnpipeline","abstract":[{"text":"What happens between the player pressing Return and the next prompt.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline","type":"topic","kind":"article"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/MapEntry":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MapEntry"}],"role":"symbol","title":"MapEntry","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/mapentry","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MapEntry"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"One statement in a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map"},{"type":"text","text":" block: an exit, a blocked exit, an initial item"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"placement, or the player’s starting location."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/MapEntry","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Item/isHeld":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/isHeld","abstract":[{"text":"True if the player is carrying the item (including worn items).","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"isHeld","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/item\/isheld","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"isHeld"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Item/==(_:_:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/item\/==(_:_:)","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/==(_:_:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"=="},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Item","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto4ItemV"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Item","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto4ItemV"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}],"kind":"symbol","tit